2	engineering	{\n        "hero": {\n            "title": "Engineering & Technology Career Guide",\n            "subtitle": "Courses, Entrance Exams, Colleges & Career Scope — A Complete Roadmap",\n            "description": "Planning a career in engineering can feel overwhelming — B.Tech, Diploma, Polytechnic, dozens of branches, entrance exams like JEE Main, WBJEE, IIT vs NIT vs state colleges, and counselling rounds. This page brings everything together in one place.",\n            "description2": "Whether you're exploring options after Class 10 (Polytechnic route) or preparing seriously after Class 12 (PCM) for a B.Tech degree, you'll find clear pathways, branch choices, exam guidance, college types, and direct links to detailed pages across the portal — so you can plan your next step with confidence.",\n            "heroStats": [\n                {\n                    "icon": "ClipboardList",\n                    "label": "Most common entrance",\n                    "value": "JEE Main / WBJEE"\n                },\n                {\n                    "icon": "BadgeCheck",\n                    "label": "Need guidance?",\n                    "value": "Counselor Support"\n                }\n            ],\n            "quickLinks": [\n                {\n                    "desc": "Step-by-step pathway after 12 for B.Tech/B.E.",\n                    "href": "/careers/after-class-12-engineering",\n                    "icon": "GraduationCap",\n                    "title": "After Class 12 • Engineering"\n                },\n                {\n                    "desc": "3-year diploma after Class 10 — job-ready fast.",\n                    "href": "/courses/diploma-in-engineering-polytechnic",\n                    "icon": "Wrench",\n                    "title": "Polytechnic / Diploma"\n                },\n                {\n                    "desc": "All B.Tech/B.E. branches and specialisations.",\n                    "href": "/courses/btech-be-programs",\n                    "icon": "Cpu",\n                    "title": "B.Tech Programs"\n                },\n                {\n                    "desc": "Top national institutes and admission routes.",\n                    "href": "/colleges/iits-indian-institutes-of-technology",\n                    "icon": "Building2",\n                    "title": "IITs / NITs / IIITs"\n                }\n            ]\n        },\n        "primaryExam": {\n            "heading": "JEE: The Main Engineering Entrance Exam",\n            "intro": "JEE (Joint Entrance Examination) is the primary national-level entrance used for admission into B.Tech / B.E. programmes at NITs, IIITs, GFTIs, and hundreds of state and private engineering colleges. JEE Advanced — attempted only by top JEE Main scorers — is the sole gateway to the IITs. If your goal is a quality engineering seat, especially in a government or centrally-funded institute, JEE preparation is your most important step.",\n            "quickFacts": [\n                {\n                    "label": "Subjects",\n                    "value": "Physics • Chemistry • Mathematics"\n                },\n                {\n                    "label": "Question Type",\n                    "value": "MCQ + Numerical (CBT)"\n                },\n                {\n                    "label": "Used For",\n                    "value": "UG Engineering Admissions"\n                }\n            ],\n            "purpose": "Admission to B.Tech / B.E. at NITs, IIITs, and GFTIs (JEE Main). Top scorers in JEE Main qualify for JEE Advanced — the only route to IIT admissions. Many state and private colleges also accept JEE Main scores directly or use it as a benchmark.",\n            "eligibility": [\n                {\n                    "category": "General Category",\n                    "details": "Passed Class 12 with Physics, Chemistry & Mathematics. Maximum 2 consecutive attempts from the year of passing"\n                },\n                {\n                    "category": "SC / ST / PWD",\n                    "details": "Passed Class 12 with PCM. Relaxation in qualifying marks as per NTA norms"\n                },\n                {\n                    "category": "JEE Advanced",\n                    "details": "Must be in top 2.5 lakh of JEE Main. Maximum 2 attempts in consecutive years"\n                }\n            ],\n            "applyMode": "Online Application Mode (NTA)",\n            "officialWebsite": "https://jeemain.nta.nic.in/",\n            "advancedWebsite": "https://jeeadv.ac.in/",\n            "unlocksDescription": "JEE is not just 'one exam' — it is a tiered gateway to multiple engineering pathways. Your JEE Main score opens doors to NITs, IIITs, and state colleges, while a top score in JEE Advanced gives access to the IITs — India's most prestigious engineering institutions.",\n            "unlocks": [\n                "NITs (National Institutes of Technology) — centrally funded, excellent placements across all branches",\n                "IIITs (Information Technology Institutes) — strong in CSE/IT and related fields",\n                "GFTIs (Govt. Funded Technical Institutes) — affordable, quality engineering education",\n                "IITs (via JEE Advanced) — top-ranked globally, strongest research and industry connections",\n                "State and private colleges that accept JEE Main as a qualifying or direct admission score"\n            ],\n            "stateExams": {\n                "title": "Also relevant: WBJEE (West Bengal State Exam)",\n                "description": "WBJEE is conducted by the West Bengal Joint Entrance Examinations Board for admission to B.Tech / B.E. programmes in state universities and private engineering colleges in West Bengal. Students from West Bengal should plan for both JEE Main and WBJEE simultaneously — the syllabi overlap significantly and preparing for one strengthens the other."\n            },\n            "whoShouldFocusIntro": "JEE rewards consistent, concept-based preparation. It is best suited for students who are strong in Mathematics and willing to practise problem-solving regularly over a 1–2 year preparation cycle.",\n            "whoShouldFocusPoints": [\n                "You enjoy problem-solving in Physics and Mathematics",\n                "You can maintain a steady daily study routine for 12–24 months",\n                "You are aiming for a government or top-ranked engineering college",\n                "You can handle concept-heavy questions and timed mock tests without losing focus"\n            ],\n            "prepPlan": [\n                {\n                    "title": "Clear your Class 11 concepts first — the base matters most",\n                    "description": "Most JEE failures happen because Class 11 concepts (especially in Physics and Mathematics) are weak. Before moving to advanced topics or extra materials, make sure your Class 11 NCERT and basic problem-solving foundation is solid."\n                },\n                {\n                    "title": "Daily problem practice — vary the difficulty level",\n                    "description": "Solve problems from all three subjects every day. Start with medium-level questions, then gradually add harder ones. Do not skip Chemistry — it is the most scoring subject and the easiest to improve quickly with regular revision."\n                },\n                {\n                    "title": "Full-length mock tests — start early, analyse every attempt",\n                    "description": "Attempt a full-length mock at least once every two weeks in the first year, then increase frequency closer to the exam. Spend more time on post-test analysis than on the test itself — understanding why an answer was wrong is where real improvement happens."\n                },\n                {\n                    "title": "Track weak topics — fix them before they compound",\n                    "description": "Keep a running list of topics where you consistently lose marks. Revisit them weekly. In JEE, negative marking means that guessing on weak topics costs you more than skipping. Knowing your weak areas and managing them is as important as mastering your strong ones."\n                }\n            ]\n        },\n        "pathways": {\n            "title": "Choose Your Engineering Pathway",\n            "subtitle": "Pick your stage, then follow the most realistic path based on eligibility and exam requirements.",\n            "after10": {\n                "title": "After Class 10th",\n                "description": "If you have completed Class 10, the Polytechnic / Diploma in Engineering route is the most practical early entry into the engineering field. It is a 3-year programme that gives you job-ready technical skills and also acts as a bridge to B.Tech (lateral entry) later.",\n                "points": [\n                    "Best for: Students who want early employment or are not yet ready for the JEE route",\n                    "Good options: Diploma in Engineering (Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, Electronics, Computer Science)",\n                    "Next step: Choose a trade + shortlist polytechnic colleges + check scholarship options"\n                ],\n                "links": [\n                    {\n                        "label": "Diploma in Engineering (Polytechnic)",\n                        "meta": "Entry route",\n                        "href": "/courses/diploma-in-engineering-polytechnic"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "label": "Polytechnic Colleges",\n                        "meta": "Colleges",\n                        "href": "/colleges/polytechnic-colleges"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "label": "After Class 10 Career Guidance",\n                        "meta": "Stage",\n                        "href": "/careers/after-class-10"\n                    }\n                ]\n            },\n            "after12": {\n                "title": "After Class 12th",\n                "description": "The standard route to an engineering degree starts after Class 12 with PCM (Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics). JEE Main is the primary entrance exam, with WBJEE for West Bengal state seats. Your rank determines the college and branch you can get.",\n                "points": [\n                    "Best for: PCM students targeting a B.Tech/B.E. degree from a good institute",\n                    "Exam reality: JEE Main for NITs/IIITs/GFTIs; JEE Advanced for IITs; WBJEE for WB state colleges",\n                    "Backup-smart: Build Plan A (IIT/NIT via JEE), Plan B (state college via WBJEE), Plan C (private college direct admission)"\n                ],\n                "links": [\n                    {\n                        "label": "After Class 12 • Engineering",\n                        "meta": "Stage",\n                        "href": "/careers/after-class-12-engineering"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "label": "B.Tech / B.E Programs",\n                        "meta": "UG",\n                        "href": "/courses/btech-be-programs"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "label": "National Level Exams",\n                        "meta": "Exams",\n                        "href": "/exams/national-level-eg-jee-main-jee-advanced"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "label": "State Level Exams (WBJEE)",\n                        "meta": "Exams",\n                        "href": "/exams/state-level-wbjee-etc"\n                    }\n                ]\n            }\n        },\n        "courseBranches": {\n            "title": "Courses & Branches",\n            "subtitle": "Understand what each course family leads to, and which one matches your interest + strengths.",\n            "intro": "Engineering is not one career — it is a wide field with dozens of branches. The most in-demand tracks today span computer science, electronics, mechanical, civil, and electrical — but newer areas like data science, AI, and mechatronics are growing fast. Choose based on what genuinely interests you, not just current placement trends.",\n            "cards": [\n                {\n                    "icon": "Cpu",\n                    "title": "Core Engineering — B.Tech / B.E.",\n                    "description": "The standard 4-year undergraduate degree. Branches include Computer Science, Electronics, Mechanical, Civil, Electrical, Chemical, and more.",\n                    "points": [\n                        "Best for: Students targeting IITs / NITs / good private colleges with strong placements",\n                        "Main gate: JEE Main (NITs/IIITs) · JEE Advanced (IITs) · WBJEE (WB state)",\n                        "Outcome: Engineer, software developer, analyst, researcher, or higher studies (M.Tech/MBA)"\n                    ],\n                    "links": [\n                        {\n                            "label": "B.Tech / B.E Programs",\n                            "href": "/courses/btech-be-programs"\n                        },\n                        {\n                            "label": "M.Tech (PG)",\n                            "meta": "PG",\n                            "href": "/courses/mtech"\n                        }\n                    ]\n                },\n                {\n                    "icon": "Wrench",\n                    "title": "Polytechnic / Diploma (Early Entry)",\n                    "description": "A 3-year diploma after Class 10 that provides practical, job-oriented technical training. Also serves as a lateral entry pathway into B.Tech (2nd year) later.",\n                    "points": [\n                        "Best for: Students who want early employment or want to enter engineering without the JEE pressure",\n                        "Outcome: Junior engineer, technician, site supervisor, or B.Tech via lateral entry",\n                        "Good for: Faster employment vs the 4-year B.Tech route"\n                    ],\n                    "links": [\n                        {\n                            "label": "Diploma in Engineering (Polytechnic)",\n                            "href": "/courses/diploma-in-engineering-polytechnic"\n                        },\n                        {\n                            "label": "Polytechnic Colleges",\n                            "href": "/colleges/polytechnic-colleges"\n                        }\n                    ]\n                },\n                {\n                    "icon": "Code",\n                    "title": "CS, IT & Computer Applications",\n                    "description": "Beyond B.Tech CSE, there are BCA, B.Sc CS/IT, and MCA pathways that lead to software and tech careers — suitable even for students from non-PCM backgrounds.",\n                    "points": [\n                        "Best for: Students interested in software, data, AI, web development, or IT",\n                        "Note: BCA / B.Sc CS are good alternatives if JEE is not the plan",\n                        "PG option: MCA / M.Sc CS/IT for specialisation"\n                    ],\n                    "links": [\n                        {\n                            "label": "BCA",\n                            "href": "/courses/bca"\n                        },\n                        {\n                            "label": "B.Sc Computer Science / IT",\n                            "href": "/courses/bsc-computer-science-it"\n                        },\n                        {\n                            "label": "MCA",\n                            "meta": "PG",\n                            "href": "/courses/mca"\n                        }\n                    ]\n                },\n                {\n                    "icon": "PenTool",\n                    "title": "Architecture & Design",\n                    "description": "B.Arch is a 5-year professional degree combining engineering and design. Admission is via JEE Main (Paper 2) or NATA. It leads to careers in architecture, urban planning, and construction.",\n                    "points": [\n                        "Best for: Students with interest in design, space planning, and built environments",\n                        "Main gate: JEE Main Paper 2 / NATA",\n                        "Outcome: Architect, urban planner, interior designer"\n                    ],\n                    "links": [\n                        {\n                            "label": "B.Arch",\n                            "href": "/courses/barch"\n                        },\n                        {\n                            "label": "Architecture Exams (NATA / AAT)",\n                            "href": "/exams/architecture"\n                        }\n                    ]\n                }\n            ]\n        },\n        "colleges": {\n            "title": "Colleges & Institutes",\n            "subtitle": "Shortlist colleges by institute type, branch availability, location, and affordability.",\n            "intro": "When choosing an engineering college, focus on: AICTE/UGC recognition, placement records for your target branch, lab and infrastructure quality, and total cost of attendance (fees + hostel + exam/counselling expenses). Tier of the institute matters for first jobs — but consistent academic performance matters more for long-term careers.",\n            "listings": [\n                {\n                    "label": "IITs — Indian Institutes of Technology",\n                    "href": "/colleges/iits-indian-institutes-of-technology",\n                    "meta": "National"\n                },\n                {\n                    "label": "NITs — National Institutes of Technology",\n                    "href": "/colleges/nits-national-institutes-of-technology",\n                    "meta": "National"\n                },\n                {\n                    "label": "IIITs — Information Technology Institutes",\n                    "href": "/colleges/iits-indian-institutes-of-technology",\n                    "meta": "National"\n                },\n                {\n                    "label": "Engineering Colleges",\n                    "href": "/colleges/engineering-colleges",\n                    "meta": "By Field"\n                },\n                {\n                    "label": "Polytechnic Colleges (Diploma)",\n                    "href": "/colleges/polytechnic-colleges",\n                    "meta": "Diploma"\n                }\n            ],\n            "checklist": [\n                "Is the institute AICTE-approved and university-affiliated?",\n                "Placement records for your specific branch (not just overall)",\n                "Lab quality, industry tie-ups, and internship support",\n                "Total cost: fees + hostel + commute + equipment",\n                "Location and connectivity — affects internship and job opportunities"\n            ]\n        }\n    }	t	2026-07-25 19:12:07	2026-07-26 17:54:10	/career/by-profession/engineering
